 {
   "id": "grammar.b1.centroamerica.01.una-vez-que",
-  "title": "Una vez que: marcar el punto de partida de algo nuevo",
+  "title": "The pluperfect: what had already happened",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "content": "*Una vez que* (once, as soon as) marks the moment one thing is complete and something new begins as a result -- useful for historical narration moving from a turning-point event into what followed. It takes the indicative for a completed past event, the subjunctive for a future or hypothetical one. These sentences are taken directly from the previous reading."
