+          "english": "Letelier was a politician whose campaign against Pinochet was very well known."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Estos archivos permitieron, por medio de un análisis cuidadoso, reconstruir el destino de miles de víctimas.",
-          "english": "These archives allowed, by means of careful analysis, the fate of thousands of victims to be reconstructed."
+          "spanish": "Los archivos, cuyo hallazgo en 1992 cambió la investigación, mostraban la coordinación entre las policías.",
+          "english": "The archives, whose discovery in 1992 changed the investigation, showed the coordination between the police forces."
         },
         {
-          "spanish": "Las distintas agencias de inteligencia se comunicaban por medio de una red de radio compartida entre los países participantes.",
-          "english": "The various intelligence agencies communicated by means of a shared radio network among the participating countries."
+          "spanish": "Eran dictaduras cuyos servicios de inteligencia compartían información.",
+          "english": "They were dictatorships whose intelligence services shared information."
         }
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "*Por medio de* is more concrete than *mediante* -- reach for it specifically when naming a tangible mechanism (a document, a network, an agreement) rather than an abstract method."
+      "content": "Do not put an article after *cuyo*: *cuyo objetivo*, not *cuyo el objetivo*. Do not replace it with *que su*: *una red que su objetivo era…* is a common mistake."
